error[E0301]: `Box` is a variant of `Shape`, and a variant value is spelled with its enum
 --> mem:///main.lu:7:16
  |
3 |     Box(int),
  |     --- `Box` is declared here, in `Shape`
...
7 |     if n > 0 { Box(n) } else { Dot }
  |                ^^^ write `Shape.Box`
  |
  = note: a variant belongs to its enum, so a value names both: `Shape.Box`. A bare capitalized
    name is how an error-row tag is spelled, which is why this one did not resolve. In a
    `match` arm the bare name is fine: the scrutinee's type already says which enum.
help: write `Shape.Box`
  |
7 |     if n > 0 { Shape.Box(n) } else { Dot }
  |

